{"timeLimit":2400,"questions":[{"question":"Evaluate \\(403_{\\text{five}} + 1013_{\\text{five}}\\).","options":["\\(10123_{\\text{five}}\\)","\\(10321_{\\text{five}}\\)","\\(10231_{\\text{five}}\\)","\\(10331_{\\text{five}}\\)","\\(1421_{\\text{five}}\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(403_{\\text{five}} = 103\\) and \\(1013_{\\text{five}} = 133\\); \\(103 + 133 = 236\\).","\\(236 = 1 \\times 125 + 4 \\times 25 + 2 \\times 5 + 1 = 1421_{\\text{five}}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Number Bases","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Corresponding sides of two similar triangles are in the ratio \\(2 : 3\\). If the area of the small triangle is \\(48\\text{ cm}^{2}\\), then the area of the large triangle is:","options":["\\(230\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)","\\(106\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)","\\(107\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)","\\(108\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)","\\(200\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Areas are in the ratio \\(2^{2} : 3^{2} = 4 : 9\\).","\\(48 \\times \\frac{9}{4} = 108\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Similarity","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"If \\(a = 2b - c\\), find the value of \\(b\\) when \\(a = 11\\) and \\(c = 23\\).","options":["\\(17\\)","\\(7\\)","\\(8\\)","\\(14\\)","\\(16\\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(11 = 2b - 23\\), so \\(2b = 34\\) and \\(b = 17\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Algebra","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the simple interest on \\(₦30,000.00\\) for \\(3\\tfrac{1}{2}\\) years at \\(5\\%\\) per annum.","options":["\\(₦5,250.00\\)","\\(₦5,775.00\\)","\\(₦10,750.00\\)","\\(₦11,550.00\\)","\\(₦15,770.00\\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(\\frac{30\\,000 \\times 5 \\times 3.5}{100} = ₦5,250\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Simple Interest","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The following numbers are prime numbers EXCEPT","options":["\\(100\\)","\\(11\\)","\\(13\\)","\\(7\\)","\\(2\\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(100 = 2^{2} \\times 5^{2}\\) is not prime.","\\(11, 13, 7\\) and \\(2\\) are all prime."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Prime Numbers","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the sum of the prime factors of \\(84\\).","options":["\\(4\\)","\\(6\\)","\\(8\\)","\\(10\\)","\\(12\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(84 = 2^{2} \\times 3 \\times 7\\); the prime factors are \\(2, 3, 7\\).","\\(2 + 3 + 7 = 12\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Prime Factors","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Rohan bought a bike for \\(\\$75000\\). He wants to sell it making a \\(20\\%\\) profit. What is the selling price of the bike?","options":["\\(\\$5000\\)","\\(\\$60000\\)","\\(\\$80000\\)","\\(\\$90000\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(120\\%\\) of \\(75\\,000 = \\$90\\,000\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Profit and Loss","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The cost price of a shirt is \\(\\$2500\\). The shopkeeper sold \\(10\\) shirts at \\(15\\%\\) profit. What is the total profit made?","options":["\\(\\$1750\\)","\\(\\$4500\\)","\\(\\$1500\\)","\\(\\$2500\\)","\\(\\$3750\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Profit on one shirt \\(= 15\\%\\) of \\(2500 = \\$375\\).","On \\(10\\) shirts: \\(\\$3750\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Profit and Loss","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"If \\(\\alpha + \\beta = 90^{\\circ}\\) and \\(\\alpha : \\beta = 2 : 1\\), then what is the ratio of \\(\\cos\\alpha\\) to \\(\\cos\\beta\\)?","options":["\\(1 : 3\\)","\\(\\sqrt{3} : 1\\)","\\(1 : \\sqrt{3}\\)","\\(1 : 2\\)","None of the above"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(\\alpha = 60^{\\circ}\\), \\(\\beta = 30^{\\circ}\\).","\\(\\cos 60^{\\circ} : \\cos 30^{\\circ} = \\frac{1}{2} : \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = 1 : \\sqrt{3}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Trigonometry","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The diagonals of a rhombus are \\(16\\text{ cm}\\) and \\(12\\text{ cm}\\) in length. The length of a side of the rhombus is:","options":["\\(20\\text{ cm}\\)","\\(8\\text{ cm}\\)","\\(7\\text{ cm}\\)","\\(12\\text{ cm}\\)","\\(10\\text{ cm}\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["The diagonals bisect each other at right angles: half-diagonals \\(8\\) and \\(6\\).","Side \\(= \\sqrt{8^{2} + 6^{2}} = 10\\text{ cm}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Pythagoras","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the H.C.F. of \\(108\\) and \\(72\\).","options":["\\(9\\)","\\(18\\)","\\(27\\)","\\(36\\)","\\(72\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(108 = 2^{2} \\times 3^{3}\\), \\(72 = 2^{3} \\times 3^{2}\\); HCF \\(= 2^{2} \\times 3^{2} = 36\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"HCF and LCM","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the median of the given data: \\(13, 16, 12, 14, 19, 12, 14, 13, 14\\).","options":["\\(12\\)","\\(14\\)","\\(15\\)","\\(16\\)","\\(17\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["In order: \\(12, 12, 13, 13, 14, 14, 14, 16, 19\\).","The middle (5th) value is \\(14\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Statistics","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"What is the value of the digit \\(5\\) in the number \\(624.95\\)?","options":["5 hundreds","5 tens","5 units","5 tenths","5 hundredths"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["The \\(5\\) is in the second place after the point: hundredths."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Place Value","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Which of the following is not a quadratic equation?","options":["\\(x^{2} + 3x - 5 = 0\\)","\\(x^{2} + x^{2} + 2 = 0\\)","\\(3 + x + x^{2} = 0\\)","\\(x^{2} - 9 = 0\\)","None of the above"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Each equation has \\(x^{2}\\) as its highest power (B is \\(2x^{2} + 2 = 0\\)), so all are quadratic."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Quadratic Equations","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The following number is in base two: \\(111001\\). What is its value in base ten?","options":["\\(22\\)","\\(39\\)","\\(57\\)","\\(114\\)","\\(41\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(32 + 16 + 8 + 1 = 57\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Number Bases","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"In binary arithmetic, calculate \\(11010 - 1101\\).","options":["\\(101\\)","\\(1011\\)","\\(1101\\)","\\(10101\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(26 - 13 = 13 = 1101_{\\text{two}}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Number Bases","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The diagram is a pie chart showing the proportion of space given to topics in a health magazine. What fraction of the magazine was given to diet and exercise topics?","options":["\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{7}{12}\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Diet \\(120^{\\circ}\\) + exercise \\(90^{\\circ}\\) \\(= 210^{\\circ}\\).","\\(\\frac{210}{360} = \\frac{7}{12}\\)."],"hint":"","image":"/exam-archive/competitions/scholastic/junior-secondary/3rd-edition/first-Round/q17.svg","topic":"Pie Charts","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The ratio of the present ages of Naomi and Amina is \\(3 : 2\\). Which of the following cannot be the ratio of their ages \\(20\\) years ago?","options":["\\(17 : 10\\)","\\(7 : 5\\)","\\(8 : 5\\)","\\(11 : 7\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Ages now \\(3x\\) and \\(2x\\); \\(20\\) years ago \\(3x - 20\\) and \\(2x - 20\\).","For \\(7 : 5\\): \\(5(3x - 20) = 7(2x - 20)\\) gives \\(x = -40\\), impossible. The others give \\(x = 35, 60, 80\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Ratio","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The ratio of the present ages of Meena and Sina is \\(4 : 3\\). After \\(6\\) years, Meena's age will become \\(26\\) years. What is the present age of Sina?","options":["12 years","19 years 6 months","15 years","21 years","30 years"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Meena is \\(26 - 6 = 20\\) now, so \\(4x = 20\\) and \\(x = 5\\).","Sina is \\(3 \\times 5 = 15\\) years."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Ratio","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Mode is the ______","options":["Middle most frequent value","Least frequent value","Maximum frequent value","None of the above"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["The mode is the value that occurs most often."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Statistics","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"A clinic vaccinated \\(270\\) children in \\(3\\) consecutive days. How many children could it vaccinate in \\(5\\) days?","options":["\\(162\\)","\\(540\\)","\\(300\\)","\\(350\\)","\\(450\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(270 \\div 3 = 90\\) a day; \\(90 \\times 5 = 450\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Proportion","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The sum of three consecutive even numbers is \\(72\\). The median of these three numbers is:","options":["\\(12\\)","\\(14\\)","\\(22\\)","\\(24\\)","\\(26\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["The numbers are \\(22, 24, 26\\); the median is \\(24\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Statistics","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find one-sixth of the positive difference between \\(36\\) and \\(63\\).","options":["\\(2\\)","\\(2.5\\)","\\(3.5\\)","\\(4.5\\)","\\(5.0\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(63 - 36 = 27\\); \\(27 \\div 6 = 4.5\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Number","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Which one of the following angles can be constructed using ruler and compasses only?","options":["\\(115^{\\circ}\\)","\\(125^{\\circ}\\)","\\(135^{\\circ}\\)","\\(145^{\\circ}\\)","\\(155^{\\circ}\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(135^{\\circ} = 90^{\\circ} + 45^{\\circ}\\), both constructible by bisecting."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Construction","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Which of the following are factors of \\(6a^{2} - 2ab - 3ab + b^{2}\\)? I \\((3a - b)\\) II \\((2a + b)\\) III \\((2a - b)\\)","options":["I only","I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","None of them"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(2a(3a - b) - b(3a - b) = (3a - b)(2a - b)\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Factorisation","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"In the expansion of \\((x - 2)(x + 9)\\), what is the coefficient of \\(x\\)?","options":["\\(-18\\)","\\(-2\\)","\\(+1\\)","\\(+7\\)","\\(+9\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(x^{2} + 9x - 2x - 18 = x^{2} + 7x - 18\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Expansion","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The exact value of \\(285^{2} - 215^{2}\\) is","options":["\\(70\\)","\\(140\\)","\\(5000\\)","\\(49000\\)","\\(35000\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Difference of two squares: \\((285 - 215)(285 + 215) = 70 \\times 500 = 35\\,000\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Difference of Two Squares","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"If \\(x^{2} + 14x + k\\) is a perfect square, then \\(k =\\)","options":["\\(4\\)","\\(7\\)","\\(28\\)","\\(49\\)","\\(196\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(k = \\left(\\frac{14}{2}\\right)^{2} = 49\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Completing the Square","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"When a sum of money is shared between \\(40\\) people, they each get \\(₦800\\). If the same money is shared equally between \\(50\\) people, how much will each get?","options":["\\(₦600\\)","\\(₦640\\)","\\(₦810\\)","\\(₦960\\)","\\(₦1000\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Total \\(= 40 \\times 800 = ₦32\\,000\\); \\(32\\,000 \\div 50 = ₦640\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Proportion","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Expand the brackets and hence solve the equation \\((4a + 3)(a - 2) - (2a - 3)(2a + 3) = 0\\).","options":["\\(2\\)","\\(0.6\\)","\\(0.4\\)","\\(-2\\)","\\(-3\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\((4a^{2} - 5a - 6) - (4a^{2} - 9) = -5a + 3 = 0\\).","\\(a = 0.6\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Algebra","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the product of the L.C.M. and H.C.F. of the numbers \\(9\\), \\(12\\) and \\(18\\).","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(108\\)","accept":["108"],"explanation":["LCM \\(= 36\\), HCF \\(= 3\\); \\(36 \\times 3 = 108\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"HCF and LCM","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"A bag contains \\(3\\) black, \\(5\\) white and \\(7\\) yellow balls. If a ball is picked, what is the probability that it is either black or white?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(\\frac{8}{15}\\)","accept":["8/15"],"explanation":["\\(\\frac{3 + 5}{15} = \\frac{8}{15}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Probability","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"The sum of the roots of the quadratic equation \\(3x^{2} - 9x + 5 = 0\\) is","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(3\\)","accept":["3"],"explanation":["Sum of roots \\(= -\\frac{b}{a} = \\frac{9}{3} = 3\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Quadratic Equations","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"Calculate the value of \\(x\\) in the diagram.","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(x = 73\\)","accept":["x = 73"],"explanation":["A hexagon's angles add up to \\(720^{\\circ}\\).","\\(135 + 115 + 105 + 2x + x + 2x = 720\\), so \\(5x = 365\\) and \\(x = 73\\)."],"hint":"","image":"/exam-archive/competitions/scholastic/junior-secondary/3rd-edition/first-Round/q34.svg","topic":"Polygons","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"State the bearing of \\(W\\) from \\(O\\).","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(158^{\\circ}\\)","accept":["158°"],"explanation":["\\(V\\) is \\(81^{\\circ}\\) clockwise from North and \\(W\\) a further \\(77^{\\circ}\\).","\\(81 + 77 = 158^{\\circ}\\)."],"hint":"","image":"/exam-archive/competitions/scholastic/junior-secondary/3rd-edition/first-Round/q35.svg","topic":"Bearings","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"I think of a number, add \\(14\\) to the number and multiply the result by \\(3\\). If my final answer is \\(51\\), what number did I think of?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(3\\)","accept":["3"],"explanation":["\\(3(n + 14) = 51\\), so \\(n + 14 = 17\\) and \\(n = 3\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Algebra","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"A trapezium has an area of \\(135\\text{ m}^{2}\\). Its two parallel sides are \\(19\\text{ m}\\) and \\(d\\text{ m}\\) long and the distance between them is \\(9\\text{ m}\\). Find the value of \\(d\\).","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(d = 11\\)","accept":["d = 11"],"explanation":["\\(\\frac{1}{2}(19 + d) \\times 9 = 135\\), so \\(19 + d = 30\\) and \\(d = 11\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Mensuration","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"If \\(9 = \\frac{x - 4}{z^{2}}\\), find \\(z\\) when \\(x = 40\\).","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(z = \\pm 2\\)","accept":["±2","2 or -2","-2 or 2","2, -2","-2, 2"],"explanation":["\\(9z^{2} = 36\\), so \\(z^{2} = 4\\) and \\(z = \\pm 2\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Algebra","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"The triangles are similar. Hence calculate the length of side \\(MN\\), given that \\(XY = 8\\text{ cm}\\).","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(7.5\\text{ km}\\)","accept":["7.5 km"],"explanation":["Matching angles: \\(X \\leftrightarrow L\\) (\\(82^{\\circ}\\)), \\(Z \\leftrightarrow M\\) (\\(62^{\\circ}\\)), \\(Y \\leftrightarrow N\\) (\\(36^{\\circ}\\)).","\\(LN = 6\\text{ km}\\) matches \\(XY = 8\\text{ cm}\\), so the scale is \\(\\frac{6}{8}\\).","\\(MN\\) matches \\(YZ = 10\\text{ cm}\\): \\(MN = 10 \\times \\frac{6}{8} = 7.5\\text{ km}\\)."],"hint":"","image":"/exam-archive/competitions/scholastic/junior-secondary/3rd-edition/first-Round/q39.svg","topic":"Similarity","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"A shop sells coffee in similar small and large jars. The small jars are of height \\(9\\text{ cm}\\) and diameter \\(6\\text{ cm}\\). If the radius of the large jar is \\(5\\text{ cm}\\), calculate its height.","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(15\\text{ cm}\\)","accept":["15 cm"],"explanation":["Small radius \\(= 3\\text{ cm}\\); scale factor \\(= \\frac{5}{3}\\).","Height \\(= 9 \\times \\frac{5}{3} = 15\\text{ cm}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Similarity","type":"subjective","section":null}]}